 18% and Norvane's up 12%.\n- Pellham has a C$900M transformer tender due to award in Q1 2027. Norvane has a C$450M tender in Q2. VLTX holdings won 60% of the last round.\n- VLTX holdings' utility order intake has risen every quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$670M in 2026Q3.\n\n**Data centres (n6)**\n- Growth is slowing. Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, which is slower than in 2026 because power availability limits new sites.\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres make up 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months. That backlog will need substations and transformers as projects connect.\n- The evidence is indirect. There is no direct data on data-centre equipment orders.\n\n**Risks**\n- The utility figures are plans and tenders, not awards. Funding is the main risk. n3's debt-market result (n7) says debt markets are open to Norvane but shaky for Pellham, which is the larger buyer and runs the Q1 2027 tender. n3's equity-market question (n8) was still running when I finished, so I haven't included it.\n- Data-centre equipment orders could slip later or be capped, because of the 26-month wait and the power constraints.\n- I couldn't find the VLTX customer-mix document, so I don't know how much of VLTX's orders depend on Pellham.","ttft_ms":3619,"type":"result","duration_ms":62499,"uuid":"1e52eb1e-4ee4-4682-b88c-64f53b105d4e","ttft_stream_ms":2170,"time_to_request_ms":83,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":17,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":6,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop